{"slug":"count-palindromic-subsequences","title":"Count the Palindromic Subsequences by Position","topic":"dp","difficulty":"hard","order":789,"tags":["dp","interval-dp","palindrome","counting"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Inclusion and exclusion over an interval: count without the left end, without the right end, and correct the overlap","body":["Count the **non-empty palindromic subsequences** of a word, where two subsequences are different if they use different **sets of positions** (even if they spell the same palindrome). For `bccb` the answer is 9: the four single letters, `cc` and `bb`, `bcb` twice (with either `c`) and `bccb`. Print the count modulo 1 000 000 007.","Let `pal(i, j)` be the number of palindromic subsequences inside the piece `s[i..j]`. Split them by whether they use the position `i` or the position `j`: those that **do not use `i`** are counted by `pal(i + 1, j)`, those that **do not use `j`** by `pal(i, j - 1)`. The ones counted twice are those that use neither, `pal(i + 1, j - 1)`, so by inclusion and exclusion `pal(i + 1, j) + pal(i, j - 1) - pal(i + 1, j - 1)` counts all that miss at least one end. What is left are the subsequences that use **both** `i` and `j`: they exist only if `s[i] = s[j]`, and then they are the palindromes inside `i + 1 .. j - 1` (also the empty one) with the two ends added around: `pal(i + 1, j - 1) + 1`. **`pal(i, j) = pal(i + 1, j) + pal(i, j - 1) - pal(i + 1, j - 1) + (s[i] = s[j] ? pal(i + 1, j - 1) + 1 : 0)`**, with `pal(i, i) = 1`.",{"code":"pal = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\nfor i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n    pal[i][i] = 1\n    for j in range(i + 1, n):\n        inner = pal[i + 1][j - 1] if i + 1 <= j - 1 else 0\n        value = pal[i + 1][j] + pal[i][j - 1] - inner\n        if s[i] == s[j]:\n            value += inner + 1\n        pal[i][j] = value % MOD\nprint(pal[0][n - 1])"},"Counting the pieces on the left of the \"overlap\" with a minus sign is the same principle that counts the union of two sets. The table has O(n^2) cells (about a million for 1500 letters) and each takes O(1). Compare with the longest palindromic subsequence: there the table kept a maximum, here it keeps a count, and the counts need the correction term."]},"statement":["A word `s` is given. Count the non-empty subsequences of `s` that are palindromes; two subsequences are different if they use different sets of positions. Print the count modulo 1000000007."],"inputFormat":["One line with the word `s`."],"outputFormat":["Print the number of palindromic subsequences modulo 1000000007."],"constraints":["1 <= length of s <= 1500","The word consists of lowercase English letters."],"examples":[{"input":"bccb\n","output":"9\n","note":"b, c, c, b, cc, bb, bcb (twice), bccb: 9."},{"input":"ab\n","output":"2\n","note":"Only the two single letters: 2."}],"hints":["Let pal(i, j) be the number of palindromic subsequences in the piece i..j.","Count those missing the left end, those missing the right end, and subtract those missing both.","If s[i] = s[j], add the palindromes of the inner piece (and the empty one) wrapped by the two ends."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ns = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String s = next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["pal(i, j), the number of palindromic subsequences of the piece i..j, is pal(i + 1, j) + pal(i, j - 1) - pal(i + 1, j - 1), plus pal(i + 1, j - 1) + 1 when s[i] = s[j] (the palindromes that use both ends), with pal(i, i) = 1. The answer is pal(0, n - 1) modulo 1000000007."],"complexity":"Time O(n^2), space O(n^2).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ns = input().strip()\n\nMOD = 10 ** 9 + 7\nn = len(s)\npal = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\nfor i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n    pal[i][i] = 1\n    for j in range(i + 1, n):\n        inner = pal[i + 1][j - 1] if i + 1 <= j - 1 else 0\n        value = pal[i + 1][j] + pal[i][j - 1] - inner\n        if s[i] == s[j]:\n            value += inner + 1\n        pal[i][j] = value % MOD\nprint(pal[0][n - 1])\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n\n    const long long MOD = 1000000007;\n    int n = (int)s.size();\n    vector<vector<long long>> pal(n + 1, vector<long long>(n + 1, 0));\n    for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n        pal[i][i] = 1;\n        for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {\n            long long inner = (i + 1 <= j - 1) ? pal[i + 1][j - 1] : 0;\n            long long value = pal[i + 1][j] + pal[i][j - 1] - inner;\n            if (s[i] == s[j]) value += inner + 1;\n            pal[i][j] = ((value % MOD) + MOD) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << pal[0][n - 1] << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String s = next();\n\n        final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n        int n = s.length();\n        long[][] pal = new long[n + 1][n + 1];\n        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n            pal[i][i] = 1;\n            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {\n                long inner = (i + 1 <= j - 1) ? pal[i + 1][j - 1] : 0;\n                long value = pal[i + 1][j] + pal[i][j - 1] - inner;\n                if (s.charAt(i) == s.charAt(j)) value += inner + 1;\n                pal[i][j] = ((value % MOD) + MOD) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(pal[0][n - 1]);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"bccb\n","output":"9\n"},{"input":"ab\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"a\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"aa\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"aba\n","output":"5\n"},{"input":"aaa\n","output":"7\n"},{"input":"aabbaaababbbbabbbaab\n","output":"42459\n"},{"input":"accaacccbbcccaaaabacacbbaaabcbabaaaacbabcbcacaabacbabccbaccccacbaacbcaacccaacbcabcacabcbaabaaaaaacbb\n","output":"801305098\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"244453718\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"848965905\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"709489510\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"595650115\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"175556670\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"623834767\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"247669528\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"525895650\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"590561744\n"},{"input":"\n","output":"505949525\n"}]}